From: root
 <root@runnervm5mmn9.vbe0po14bteuxnpsttwp1nmvne.bx.internal.cloudapp.net>
Date: Tue, 14 Jul 2026 08:15:46 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] c-family: Add __builtin_available support inspired by Clang

Implement __builtin_available (platform version, ...) as a keyword-based
primary expression usable in C, C++, Objective-C and Objective-C++.
The semantics mirror Clang's ParseAvailabilityCheckExpr so that
existing source using the Clang extension continues to build, e.g.:

    if (__builtin_available (macos 10.10, ios 13.0, *))
        ...

A comma-separated list of platform specs (case-insensitive, with
aliases like macosx/osx/darwin mapping to macos, and anyappleos for
the generic Apple-OS sentinel) is parsed by the C and C++ front-ends
into an availability_spec list; the wildcard '*' terminating the list
is mandatory (Clang-compatible).  Unknown platforms are diagnosed at
parse time, as are duplicate specs and a missing wildcard.

Each spec is matched against the compilation target via three new
target hooks in the TARGET_C vector:

  - availability_platform_name
  - availability_min_version
  - availability_platform_id

Darwin and Android override these hooks.  When a platform matches and
its version is below the compile-time deployment floor, the expression
folds to true.  When no spec matches the target, the wildcard applies
and the expression also folds to true, matching Clang's behaviour in
clang/test/CodeGen/availability-check-anyappleos.c.

Otherwise, GCC emits a runtime call:

  - __isPlatformVersionAtLeast (platform_id, major, minor, subminor)
    on Darwin, matching the Darwin runtime; or
  - __isOSVersionAtLeast (major, minor, subminor) on Android and other
    non-Darwin targets that hook in, matching the NDK's
    libandroid_support helper which wraps android_get_device_api_level().
    See https://developer.android.com/ndk/guides/using-newer-apis.

To keep the runtime call symbol unmangled in C++, a new language hook
make_runtime_function_decl is introduced; the C++ front-end overrides
it through build_library_fn_ptr so that the FUNCTION_DECL carries
C linkage (no _Z... mangling).  Without this hook, the C++
immediate-escalation walk would also crash on a hook-built decl that
lacks DECL_LANG_SPECIFIC.

Tests cover all four front-ends and the Android codegen path (verifying
that __isOSVersionAtLeast is emitted with the unmangled symbol and
that the Darwin-specific __isPlatformVersionAtLeast helper does not
leak into non-Darwin codegen).

